STUDENTPG ENGINEERING ONBOARDING REPORT
========================================

Audit date: 2026-09-03
Audit type: Read-only repository and limited live-production audit
Repository: StudentPG

IMPORTANT SCOPE
---------------
This report is based on repository source code, configuration files, documentation, tests, and a limited live check of studentpg.in. No code was modified while preparing this report. Anything that could not be verified is marked NOT VERIFIED. Secret values are intentionally omitted.

1. PROJECT OVERVIEW
-------------------
StudentPG is a student accommodation marketplace focused on PGs and hostels in Bhopal. It connects students searching for accommodation, owners listing PG properties, and administrators reviewing listings and owner verification requests.

Main use cases:
- Public visitors browse approved PGs.
- Users search by text, city, gender, rent, category, room type, and amenities.
- Users open PG details and use phone, WhatsApp, or email contact fields when available.
- Owners register, verify email, submit identity verification, and manage PG listings.
- Administrators approve/reject owner verification and PG listings.
- Public forms submit contact and issue reports with CAPTCHA and rate limiting.

The project is not verified as a payment, booking, tenancy-agreement, real-time-chat, or rental-payment platform.

One-paragraph introduction:
StudentPG is a Next.js and Spring Boot marketplace. Next.js provides public search/detail pages and authenticated dashboards. Spring Boot provides REST APIs, validation, authentication, authorization, business logic, MongoDB access, email integration, Cloudinary integration, CAPTCHA, and rate limiting. Owners must be active and verified before creating PG listings, and listings remain private until an administrator approves them.

30-second explanation:
StudentPG is a Next.js + Spring Boot + MongoDB accommodation marketplace using JWT HttpOnly-cookie authentication, Cloudinary image storage, SMTP/Brevo email, Caffeine caching, MongoDB indexes, and public approved-listing discovery.

Current maturity verified:
- Public PG discovery and detail pages
- Owner registration/login/profile/password workflows
- Owner PG CRUD and image operations
- Admin PG moderation
- Owner identity verification
- Notifications
- CAPTCHA/rate limiting for public forms
- Backend/frontend tests and CI configuration

NOT VERIFIED:
- Production capacity or concurrent-user guarantee
- Production backup policy
- Production alerting
- Full production deployment settings
- Complete live owner/contact-data consistency

2. TECHNOLOGY STACK
-------------------
Frontend: Next.js, React, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Redux Toolkit, RTK Query, React Hook Form, Zod, Lucide React, Next Image.
Backend: Spring Boot 3.5.14, Java compiler target 17, Spring Web, Spring Security, Spring Data MongoDB, Jakarta Validation, Spring Cache, Caffeine, Actuator, Lombok, SpringDoc, JJWT 0.12.6, Spring Dotenv.
Database: MongoDB through Spring Data MongoDB.
Authentication: JWT signed with HMAC and stored in an HttpOnly access_token cookie; Bearer fallback is also supported.
Password security: BCrypt strength 12.
Image/document storage: Cloudinary.
Email: SMTP with Brevo REST API fallback.
CAPTCHA: Custom HMAC-signed arithmetic CAPTCHA.
State: Redux Toolkit and RTK Query.
Testing: JUnit/Spring Boot tests and Vitest frontend tests.
Deployment files: Dockerfiles, docker-compose.yml, backend/nginx.conf, GitHub Actions workflow.
Monitoring: Spring Actuator health endpoint and application/request logging.
Domain observed live: studentpg.in redirects to www.studentpg.in.
Actual Vercel/Render deployment settings: NOT VERIFIED.

3. SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE
----------------------
Browser
  |
  v
Next.js Frontend
  | HTTPS/REST and frontend API routes
  v
Spring Boot Backend
  |
  +--> Spring Security and JWT filter
  +--> Controllers
  +--> Services
  +--> Repositories/MongoTemplate
  +--> Caffeine cache
  |
  +--> MongoDB
  +--> Cloudinary
  +--> SMTP/Brevo

Frontend boundary:
- Renders public, owner, and admin screens.
- Calls APIs using backendClient or RTK Query.
- Contains Next.js API proxy routes.
- Uses server components for public search/detail data fetching.

Backend boundary:
- Authenticates and authorizes requests.
- Applies validation and business rules.
- Performs ownership checks.
- Reads and writes MongoDB.
- Integrates Cloudinary and email services.

Public flow:
Browser -> Next.js public page -> backend public/student endpoint -> approved PG query -> response -> UI.
Owner flow:
Owner -> login -> JWT cookie -> protected owner controller -> ownership check -> service -> MongoDB/Cloudinary.
Admin flow:
Admin -> login -> ADMIN JWT -> admin controller -> admin service -> moderation update -> notification where applicable.

